    description: "From validation drain 2026-05-21 (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05212026_1522.md). Cohort run on apollo-server (3780 nodes, 7422 edges, 102 usage_contexts).\n\nPR #3826 successfully added _extract_http_handler_contexts to js_ts.py — 13 kind=call UCs are now emitted on apollo-server for the WI-tisam target set (5 startStandaloneServer, 3 createServer, 3 http.createServer, 1 https.createServer, 1 runHttpQuery). INV-rolul confirmed moved.\n\nBut Symbols with framework_role=http_handler or http_route remain at 0. 'hypergumbo routes' on the apollo-server behavior map reports 'No API routes found'. Other framework_roles ARE detected (event_subscriber=14, graphql_resolver=150, route=1, http_client=7, graphql_client=38, mq_publisher=1) so the linker pipeline runs — it just doesn't classify these particular UCs.\n\nHypothesis: the route_handler linker (or whichever stage maps UCs to framework_role) is missing a consumer for the new kind=call UCs that _extract_http_handler_contexts emits. The fix may need to extend the linker's consumption logic to recognize these UCs and tag the corresponding call_site Symbols (or some derived Symbol) with framework_role=http_handler.\n\nSuggested investigation:\n1. Trace one of the 5 startStandaloneServer UCs — what symbol_ref does it carry, where does the linker look for it.\n2. Compare with how Express/Hapi/Next.js route patterns get from UC to framework_role (they DO produce route classifications today, per fixture tests).\n3. The YAML pattern files (node-http.yaml, graphql.yaml from #3826) define the call-name + role mapping; verify they're loaded by the linker."  # d198
    fields: {}  # d198
